                <pb facs="0566" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00 Tacoma/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-17T14:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>70. Referring to the Department’s telegram 28, August 15, 2[<hi
                        rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m. The President assured me that he will bring
                    up the boundary question at the conference and attempt to arrive at a
                    solution.</p>
                <p>In company with the President and party I shall leave for Amapala on the 18th
                    instant to attend the conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
